From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: vamos <vamos@comma.ai>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 18:00:00 -0700
Subject: ufs: qcom: disable clock gating capabilities

Boot-time UIC storm (pwr ctrl/uic cmd completion timeouts, TSTBUS
dumps, link left degraded) on the comma four roughly every other boot,
even with phy_calibrate() on resume (patch 0019). Remove the clock
gating windows entirely for bring-up.
---

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index eba0e6617..48b6a0adf 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -1159,7 +1159,12 @@ static void ufs_qcom_set_host_caps(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 
 static void ufs_qcom_set_caps(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 {
-	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_GATING | UFSHCD_CAP_HIBERN8_WITH_CLK_GATING;
+	/*
+	 * comma four (SDM845): clock gating + hibern8-with-clk-gating cause a
+	 * boot-time UIC storm (pwr ctrl/uic cmd completion timeouts, link left
+	 * broken) roughly every other boot, even with the phy_calibrate()
+	 * recalibration fix. Disable the gating windows entirely for bring-up.
+	 */
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_SCALING | UFSHCD_CAP_WB_WITH_CLK_SCALING;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_AUTO_BKOPS_SUSPEND;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_WB_EN;
